    "meal_prep": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "m_sub": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "Defrost and dry",
            "subheading_size": "subtitle-md",
            "secondary_color": true
          }
        },
        "m_head": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Rinse, shuck, pat dry, then wait",
            "heading_size": "title-md",
            "heading_tag": "h2",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Straight from the freezer, rinse the scallops under cold running water to remove the thin ice glaze. Once they loosen, gently slide each scallop off its shell with a spoon, then rinse and dry the shells for serving. Pat every scallop dry, making sure no glaze is left, set them on a fresh paper towel-lined plate and refrigerate uncovered for 1 to 2 hours, until fully defrosted. Blot away any moisture that comes out.</p><p>Pat them dry once more and season with kosher salt right before they go into the pan. A dry surface is the key to a golden crust.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "m_btn": {
          "type": "button",
          "settings": {
            "button_label": "Shop Half-Shell Scallops",
            "button_link": "/products/half-shell-scallops-2x-12oz-bag",
            "button_style": "primary",
            "button_size": "md",
            "button_external": false,
            "button_icon": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "m_sub",
        "m_head",
        "m_text",
        "m_btn"
      ],
